  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Club Website, In Your Pocket",
    "overview": "The app wears stxrobotics.com's clothes. The user chose the clickable prototype (`prototype/stx-robotics-app.html`) as the binding reference. Where it disagrees with an earlier DESIGN.md or with general craft rules, the prototype wins. The React Native port in `mobile/src` follows its CSS classes 1:1, and this file describes that port.\n\nIt reads like a clean, light editorial page shrunk to a phone. The page is light grey, cards are white with a thin border, and the ink is near-black. Maroon is the brand voice and black gives the structure. Every corner is square. Most screen tops follow the website's pattern: an uppercase eyebrow with a short rule before it, a bold heading, then a lead line. Big numbers sit in a full-bleed black band. Small uppercase letter-spaced labels (tags, chips, tab labels, section titles) do the sorting work.\n\nInformation is dense but legible. Atkinson Hyperlegible is the only typeface, in two weights plus a bold italic for the logo.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Atkinson Hyperlegible throughout, with bold headings and tight leading.",
      "Square corners on every control and container. The only rounded shapes are the SMS bubble, the printer LED, the tab badge and the desktop phone frame.",
      "White cards with 1px #e5e9f0 borders on a #f7fafc page, with no shadows inside the app.",
      "Maroon solid buttons, 1.5px black outline buttons, and black-filled selected states.",
      "Eyebrow, then heading, then lead at the top of screens. A black stats band carries the big numbers.",
      "An 18px gutter, 14px card padding, 10px stack gaps and 20px section tops."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Maroon Speaks, Black Holds Rule",
        "body": "Maroon is for brand and action: the primary button, the active state and links. Black is for structure and selection: bands, outlines, chips and the role switch. Do not swap them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Muted On Grey Rule",
        "body": "`muted` on `page` just meets 4.5:1, but on the darker `line` backdrop it does not. Text on the desktop backdrop uses the darker step #4c5d84.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tracked Caps Rule",
        "body": "Uppercase text is always 10.5 to 13px, bold (band labels are the one regular-weight case), and tracked at roughly 0.06 to 0.14em. Headings and body text are never uppercase.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Numbers Rule",
        "body": "Stats, scores, seat counts and job ids use tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Phone Rule",
        "body": "No component inside the screen casts a shadow. Separation comes from borders, tone and bands.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** open screens with eyebrow, H2 and lead, as stxrobotics.com does.",
      "**Do** put headline numbers in the black stats band with 24px bold tabular figures.",
      "**Do** group content in white cards (1px `line`, 14px padding) stacked 10px apart.",
      "**Do** use the 18px gutter, 20px section top and 10px stack gap on every screen.",
      "**Do** keep every corner square (0) except the SMS bubble, LED, badge and phone frame.",
